-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ח/2 — תשלום בגין שחיקה לעובדי הוראה לשנים 1999–2001 (10.12.2007)
-- The detailed instructions for the one-time erosion grant of the 2007
-- arbitration award: 3.5% of the determining salary for each month worked
-- in "the period", less the 0.5% advance, pro-rated and index-linked by the
-- attached table, paid with December 2007's salary.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תשלום בגין שחיקה — הנחיות לתשלום המענק החד פעמי`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 The letterhead, title, date, addressee, greeting and subject line, and the recital: the 1.2.2007 agreement sent the erosion dispute (from 1.1.1999) to arbitration, circular תשס"ז/4 carried out part of the award, and these are the Treasury's instructions of 15.11.2007 for the grant of its §3.

-- Time in this file is counted in salary months from December 2007 (0),
-- the circular's month; December's salary is paid on 1.1.2008 (month 1).
`December 2007 salary, paid 1.1.2008` MEANS 1

`the period starts` MEANS Date 1 1 2000
`the period ends`   MEANS Date 31 12 2002
`grant rate`        MEANS 3.5%
`advance rate`      MEANS 0.5%

@desc One month of the employee's work, as far as the grant asks about it.
DECLARE `work month` HAS
    `month number of the year` IS A NUMBER  @desc 1 = January
    `calendar year`            IS A NUMBER
    `actually worked`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `determining salary paid`  IS A NUMBER  @desc the determining salary actually paid for the month, already in proportion to the position fraction and the part of the month employed (§1.2)
    `advance paid`             IS A NUMBER  @desc the 0.5% advance already paid for the month; an input
    `on unpaid leave or sabbatical` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `grant action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the period` m IF
        Date 1 (m's `month number of the year`) (m's `calendar year`) AT LEAST `the period starts`
    AND Date 1 (m's `month number of the year`) (m's `calendar year`) AT MOST `the period ends`

§§ `1 כללי`

-- §1.1 and its first sub-paragraph: for each month actually worked in the
-- period, 3.5% of the determining salary less the 0.5% advance paid for it.
-- F-2007-08_tashsach_02-a: the circular's title and recital speak of 1999–
-- 2001; the period it sets is 1.1.2000–31.12.2002, and its own note says
-- that period governs.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-1 akn:art_1__para_1-1__subpara_1 akn:art_1__para_1-1__subpara_1/p2
GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month's grant before linkage` m IS
    `grant rate` TIMES m's `determining salary paid` MINUS m's `advance paid`

-- §1.1's opening: the grant is for the months actually worked in the period.
GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `worked in the period` m IF
        `in the period` m
    AND m's `actually worked`

-- §1.5: no grant for months of unpaid leave (חל"ת) or sabbatical.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-5
GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the month earns a grant` m IF
        `worked in the period` m
    AND NOT m's `on unpaid leave or sabbatical`

§§ `1.6 The linkage table`

@desc One row of the attached table of linkage coefficients to the consumer price index.
DECLARE `index month` HAS
    `table month`        IS A NUMBER
    `table year`         IS A NUMBER
    `price index`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the month's consumer price index, average 1998 = 100
    `monthly change`     IS A NUMBER  @desc the printed change from the month before, in percent
    `linkage coefficient` IS A NUMBER
    `number of months`   IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_1__para_1-6/p7
`the September 2007 index` MEANS 119.605

-- §1.6 and the attached table (¶6, the table, and its footnote ¶8: all the
-- indices on the one base, average 1998).
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-6 akn:art_1__para_1-6/p6 akn:art_1__para_1-6/t1 akn:art_1__para_1-6/p8
`the linkage table` MEANS
    LIST `index month` 1 2000 106.10 (0) 1.127 92,
         `index month` 2 2000 105.60 (-0.5) 1.133 91,
         `index month` 3 2000 105.30 (-0.3) 1.136 90,
         `index month` 4 2000 105.80 (0.5) 1.130 89,
         `index month` 5 2000 106.70 (0.9) 1.121 88,
         `index month` 6 2000 107.00 (0.3) 1.118 87,
         `index month` 7 2000 107.30 (0.3) 1.115 86,
         `index month` 8 2000 106.70 (-0.6) 1.121 85,
         `index month` 9 2000 106.10 (-0.6) 1.127 84,
         `index month` 10 2000 106.70 (0.6) 1.121 83,
         `index month` 11 2000 106.70 (0.0) 1.121 82,
         `index month` 12 2000 106.60 (-0.1) 1.122 81,
         `index month` 1 2001 105.97 (-0.6) 1.129 80,
         `index month` 2 2001 105.87 (-0.1) 1.130 79,
         `index month` 3 2001 106.08 (0.2) 1.127 78,
         `index month` 4 2001 107.04 (0.9) 1.117 77,
         `index month` 5 2001 107.46 (0.4) 1.113 76,
         `index month` 6 2001 107.78 (0.3) 1.110 75,
         `index month` 7 2001 108.21 (0.4) 1.105 74,
         `index month` 8 2001 108.53 (0.3) 1.102 73,
         `index month` 9 2001 108.74 (0.2) 1.100 72,
         `index month` 10 2001 108.85 (0.1) 1.099 71,
         `index month` 11 2001 108.21 (-0.6) 1.105 70,
         `index month` 12 2001 108.10 (-0.1) 1.106 69,
         `index month` 1 2002 109.27 (1.1) 1.095 68,
         `index month` 2 2002 110.12 (0.8) 1.086 67,
         `index month` 3 2002 110.66 (0.5) 1.081 66,
         `index month` 4 2002 112.36 (1.5) 1.064 65,
         `index month` 5 2002 113.42 (0.9) 1.055 64,
         `index month` 6 2002 114.91 (1.3) 1.041 63,
         `index month` 7 2002 115.66 (0.6) 1.034 62,
         `index month` 8 2002 115.23 (-0.4) 1.038 61,
         `index month` 9 2002 115.66 (0.4) 1.034 60,
         `index month` 10 2002 116.40 (0.6) 1.028 59,
         `index month` 11 2002 115.44 (-0.8) 1.036 58,
         `index month` 12 2002 115.12 (-0.3) 1.039 57

GIVEN mo IS A NUMBER, yr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient the table gives` mo yr IS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `linkage coefficient`)
        (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `table month` EQUALS mo AND r's `table year` EQUALS yr) `the linkage table`)

-- The table reproduces its own rule: each coefficient is the September 2007
-- index over the month's index, to three decimals; and the months column
-- counts the months from the row's month to September 2007.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD ROUND (`the September 2007 index` DIVIDED BY r's `price index` TIMES 1000) DIVIDED BY 1000
                           EQUALS r's `linkage coefficient`)
            `the linkage table`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD (2007 MINUS r's `table year`) TIMES 12 PLUS 9 MINUS r's `table month`
                           EQUALS r's `number of months`)
            `the linkage table`
#ASSERT count `the linkage table` EQUALS 36

-- §1.2: pro-rated by the position, months and pay actually received (all in
-- `determining salary paid`), plus linkage differences. The reading adopted
-- (F-2007-08_tashsach_02-b): the coefficient links the month's grant as
-- §1.1 defines it, that is net of the advance.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-2
GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month's linked grant` m IS
    IF `the month earns a grant` m
    THEN `the month's grant before linkage` m
         TIMES sum (`the coefficient the table gives` (m's `month number of the year`) (m's `calendar year`))
    ELSE 0

GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month's grant linked before the advance` m IS
    `grant rate` TIMES m's `determining salary paid`
    TIMES sum (`the coefficient the table gives` (m's `month number of the year`) (m's `calendar year`))
    MINUS m's `advance paid`

@export The one-time erosion grant for 2000–2002 owed with December 2007's salary to a teaching employee of an owning body
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF `work month` @desc the employee's months in 2000–2002
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-time grant` months IS
    sum (map `the month's linked grant` months)

-- §1.2, last sentence: the grant is not counted in the base for computing
-- any supplement.
`the grant counts in the base of supplements` MEANS FALSE

-- §1.3: no pension or provident-fund contribution or deduction on the grant,
-- except the usual rates to the continuing-education (השתלמות) funds.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-3
DECLARE `contribution` IS ONE OF
    `pension or provident-fund contribution`
    `continuing-education fund contribution`

GIVEN c IS A `contribution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contributed on the grant` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `continuing-education fund contribution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- §1.4: budget-pension retirees are entitled only if they were active in the
-- period or part of it, and for the length of their active period — the
-- months they actually worked, which `the month earns a grant` already asks.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-4
GIVEN `active in the period` IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A LIST OF `work month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a budget-pension retiree's grant` `active in the period` months IS
    IF `active in the period` THEN `the one-time grant` months ELSE 0

@ref akn:preamble/p14
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF `work month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `the grant is paid with December 2007's salary` months IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the grant` amount
          PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `the one-time grant` months
    WITHIN `December 2007 salary, paid 1.1.2008`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the grant is paid with December 2007's salary, paid on 1.1.2008"

-- The note (הערה 1): circular תשס"ז/4 printed the period as 1.1.1999–
-- 31.12.2001; the period is the one in §1.1. ¶5 is the signature, printed
-- before the table.
@ref akn:art_1__para_1-6/p2 akn:art_1__para_1-6/p3 akn:art_1__para_1-6/p4
GIVEN m IS A `work month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 1999 month earns nothing` m IF
    m's `calendar year` EQUALS 1999 IMPLIES NOT `in the period` m

-- akn:art_1__para_1-6/p5 The signature, printed between the note and the table; no rule.

-- akn:art_1 The heading "כללי"; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`the years the title names` MEANS LIST 1999, 2000, 2001
`the years the period covers` MEANS LIST 2000, 2001, 2002

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_02-a.
`the title's years and the period's years differ` MEANS
        NOT (`the years the title names` EQUALS `the years the period covers`)
    AND NOT `in the period` (`work month` WITH
                                `month number of the year` IS 6
                                `calendar year`            IS 1999
                                `actually worked`          IS TRUE
                                `determining salary paid`  IS 10000
                                `advance paid`             IS 50
                                `on unpaid leave or sabbatical` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `the title's years and the period's years differ`

-- A determining salary of 10,000 and an advance of 50 (0.5%) are
-- placeholders.
`January 2000, full month` MEANS
    `work month` WITH
        `month number of the year`      IS 1
        `calendar year`                 IS 2000
        `actually worked`               IS TRUE
        `determining salary paid`       IS 10000
        `advance paid`                  IS 50
        `on unpaid leave or sabbatical` IS FALSE

`December 2002 on sabbatical` MEANS
    `work month` WITH
        `month number of the year`      IS 12
        `calendar year`                 IS 2002
        `actually worked`               IS TRUE
        `determining salary paid`       IS 10000
        `advance paid`                  IS 50
        `on unpaid leave or sabbatical` IS TRUE

-- 3.5% of 10,000 = 350, less 50 = 300, times 1.127 = 338.1.
#ASSERT `the month's linked grant` `January 2000, full month` EQUALS 338.1
#ASSERT `the month's linked grant` `December 2002 on sabbatical` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `contributed on the grant` `pension or provident-fund contribution`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_02-b: linking before or after the advance differs.
`linking before or after the advance differs` MEANS
    NOT (`the month's linked grant` `January 2000, full month`
         EQUALS `the month's grant linked before the advance` `January 2000, full month`)
#ASSERT `linking before or after the advance differs`

#TRACE `the grant is paid with December 2007's salary` (LIST `January 2000, full month`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the grant` 338.1 AT 1
